# Kernel options the PlutoSky R2 needs on top of fishball_defconfig.
#
# A FRAGMENT, merged over the R1's configuration only when building --rev r2
# (firmware-modern/build_all.sh). fishball_defconfig itself is not touched, so
# an R1 kernel is the same kernel it was before the R2 existed here.
#
# One option, because the two boards differ in one driver:

# --- Ethernet through the FPGA -------------------------------------------
# The R2's GEM0 reaches its RTL8211F through a Xilinx gmii_to_rgmii core in the
# fabric (dts/zynq-pluto-sdr-fishball-r2.dts says how). The core has a speed
# register on the MDIO bus, at address 8, and this is the driver that writes
# the negotiated speed into it. Without it the MAC and the PHY both probe and
# nothing tells the core what speed the link came up at.
#
# It is the option the vendor's own R2 kernel adds over its R1 kernel:
# CONFIG_XILINX_GMII2RGMII=y in the R2 patch's zynq_pluto_defconfig and not in
# the R1 patch's.
CONFIG_XILINX_GMII2RGMII=y
